## 2. Completed Improvements (Recently Implemented)

### ✅ Migration of Detail Scraping & Backfill to Fast HTTP + `goquery`
* **Previous State:** 4 Selenium WebDrivers (Chrome processes) scraped individual car detail pages. Long runs accumulated V8 JavaScript heap bloat until hitting the 4 GB limit, causing GC thrashing and fatal crashes (`0xc000013a`).
* **Current State:** 
  * Replaced Chrome detail scraping with **15 concurrent HTTP worker goroutines** using Go's `net/http` and `github.com/PuerkitoBio/goquery`.
  * Replaced Seller Backfilling with **20 concurrent HTTP worker goroutines**.
  * Memory footprint dropped from **>4 GB to ~20 MB**.
  * Scraping speed increased by **~20x–30x** (detail page fetch & parse reduced to ~500ms).

